[08:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Then I walked away, and it just sat there watching. It runs on its own processor, not my computer, so my laptop can be doing nothing, and it Vialoop is still paying attention beside it. And then, the email'

[08:40] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'came in. Upload finished. Sent through the same Gmail account it had connected for itself an hour earlier. Now, here\'s the part that actually flipped me, because everything'

[08:52] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'I just showed you, an AI moving my cursor, sending my emails, touching my files, that should terrify me, right? [music] With software, just software, it would. Vialoop gives you this insurance by'

[09:05] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'having this one physical step that you have to do if there\'s something that\'s risky or that impacts you. Now, if you\'re anything like me, there\'s a question sitting in the back of your head this'

[09:17] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'whole video. I already pay for Claude. I use it every single day, so what does a box give me that a chatbot doesn\'t? And I\'ll start with a point where Claude actually wins. Claude runs on my subscription.'

[09:29] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'It\'s a flat fee that I use all day. Vialoop runs on API tokens, and tokens add up. It keeps the routine stuff local to soften that, but you actually need an'

[09:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'API token for Claude or ChatGPT to get the full potential of Vialume. But, that\'s the thing. The chat part is basically pretty similar to Claude.'

[09:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Still much smarter, in my opinion, because it learns everything about you by reading your screen constantly. But, the difference mainly is what happens after the chat. Claude waits for me to come to it. It can\'t sit there'

[10:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'watching how I work and offer something before I ask. Vialume can do things and access things that Claude doesn\'t want to, that Claude doesn\'t feel confident to do.'

[10:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'But, Vialume does it from start to finish. And the strange part is it didn\'t feel reckless because it stopped at every step that mattered and waited for my approval. And in the end, that\'s the trade. You get more capability, more'

[10:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'reach into your actual computer, but a hard physical wall in front of anything consequential. Right now, Vialume is in pre-launch. So, this is one of the very first units. And'

